{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "Synthetic printers for public Kiln's own tests. No row is a real machine and every number is made up, so the public suite never carries Kiln's catalogue: a real printer's limits, variants and spec sheet are kiln-pro's and are pinned in kiln-pro's tests. conftest installs these rows into copies of the two bundled data files (safety_profiles.json takes each row's 'safety' block, printer_intelligence.json its 'intel' block) and points the loaders at the copies for the whole session. A row with no blocks is a ROSTER-ONLY printer: it exists by name and its record is served, which is what a catalogued printer looks like to an install without kiln-pro. kilntest_variants_se is a separately catalogued prefix relative of kilntest_variants; kilntest_hot is a 500 C class machine for the adapters whose protocol ceiling sits above the desktop limits.",
    "shape": "The same two-block record kiln-pro's printer_catalogue.json carries per printer."
  },
